{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_genesis_register_genesis_register", "label": "Genesis Register \u2014 entries 1 to K", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The subject-matter record of The Lach Elemental Lattice rendered as register entries; this block becomes the opening of The Method 1.6 Register and runs up to but not including entry 165."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_three_axis_configuration_lattice", "label": "The three-axis configuration lattice (n, \u2113, k)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proposed as a theory to explore: what the conventional table conflates into one positional axis is treated as three independent axes. No new physics \u2014 only a change of coordinates."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_admissible_lattice_lambda", "label": "\u039b, the admissible lattice", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u039b = {(n,\u2113,k) : 0 \u2264 \u2113 \u2264 n\u22121, 1 \u2264 k \u2264 2(2\u2113+1)} \u2014 the angular-momentum condition and the Pauli capacity. \u2113 = 4 (g) is carried as a theoretical extension only."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_axes_are_counts_not_lengths", "label": "The axes are counts, not lengths, and they are coupled", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Distances are combinatorial, not metric, and the range of \u2113 depends on n while the range of k depends on \u2113 \u2014 which is what later permits the classification of empty space and forces register 60's dimensional obstruction."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_empty_space_partition_void_reactive_reserved", "label": "Empty space partitions into void, reactive and reserved", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The table has no vocabulary for absence; the coordinate change supplies one \u2014 void (the orbital cannot exist), reactive (capacity exceeded), reserved (permitted and simply empty)."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_census_630_cell_lattice", "label": "Census of the 630-cell lattice: 180 void \u00b7 240 reactive \u00b7 92 reserved \u00b7 118 occupied", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_reserved_recount_78_to_92", "label": "The reserved-cell recount corrects 78 \u2192 92", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both states are kept \u2014 the withdrawn 78 and the corrected 92 \u2014 rather than the earlier figure being erased."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_reserved_cells_concentrate_n6_n7", "label": "Reserved cells concentrate at n = 6\u20137 in the high-\u2113 layers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_block_structure_from_l_alone", "label": "All 118 elements place; block structure emerges from \u2113 alone", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_three_state_model", "label": "The three-state model: a ground cell and its two nearest excited neighbours", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Q\u2080 with a shell excitation Q\u2081 = (n+1,\u2113,k) and a subshell excitation Q\u2082 = (n,\u2113\u00b11,k), \u2113+1 where the angular-momentum condition permits and \u2113\u22121 otherwise."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_lach_elemental_field_equation", "label": "The Lach elemental field equation (Eq. 4)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Derived from normalisation at all t, ground-state occupancy at t = 0 and sinusoidal evolution at base frequency \u03a9."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_field_equation_is_a_construction_not_a_solution", "label": "The field equation is a construction on the lattice, not a solution of a Hamiltonian", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u03a9 is a formal parameter and the summation carries no element label, so every element shares one envelope. A caution recorded at the point of proposal \u2014 what distinguishes elements is \u0394Q and \u03c3\u00b2(t), not Eq. 4."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_displacement_vector_delta_q", "label": "The displacement vector \u0394Q and the interaction term S_Z(t)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u0394Q = Q\u2080 \u2212 \u00bd(Q\u2081+Q\u2082): the element-specific content lives in geometric quantities read off the lattice, not in the shared envelope."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_delta_q_degeneracy_two_values", "label": "|\u0394Q| is sharply degenerate, taking only two values", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1 for hydrogen and helium, 1/\u221a2 for every other element \u2014 elements are differentiated by direction, not size."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_three_geometric_classes_a_b_c", "label": "Three geometric classes by the direction of \u0394Q (A, B, C)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The classification follows entirely from \u2113 \u2264 n\u22121; the 3d series and lanthanides fall in C, the 4d and 5d series in B."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_ytterbium_platinum_adjacency", "label": "Yb and Pt are neighbours \u2014 the adjacency the conventional layout conceals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The principal structural result of Part I: the late f-block and the late 5d metals form a contiguous region the two-dimensional layout tears in half."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_hydride_formation_enthalpy_test", "label": "Hydride formation enthalpy \u0394H_f as the measured test quantity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen because it is measured, tabulated, dimensional and independent of the framework."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_two_term_regression_l_k", "label": "The two-term regression \u0394H_f = +136.2 \u2212 89.5\u2113 + 6.4k", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adding n, |Q\u2080| or H_cp gains in-sample R\u00b2 while losing it out of sample \u2014 the signature of overfitting."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_pettifor_mendeleev_number", "label": "Pettifor's Mendeleev number (prior art)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_miedema_cohesion_model", "label": "Miedema's semi-empirical cohesion model (prior art)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_benchmark_lattice_outperformed", "label": "Benchmarked against Pettifor and Miedema, the lattice is outperformed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CV R\u00b2 0.514 against 0.790 and 0.895, Wilcoxon rejecting equality \u2014 and the paper reports it rather than omitting it."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_combining_does_not_rescue", "label": "Combining the lattice with the established descriptors does not rescue it", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_occupancy_k_orthogonal", "label": "The occupancy coordinate k is orthogonal to every established descriptor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u2113 correlates strongly because it is the block label; k correlates with none, so it carries information the chemical scales do not encode."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_appending_k_raises_cv_r2", "label": "Appending k to Pettifor's scale raises CV R\u00b2 from 0.790 to 0.844", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The defensible claim is a modest contribution to an existing method, not a competitive alternative."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_delta_q_classes_separate_hydride_data", "label": "The \u0394Q direction classes separate the hydride data", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_l_term_recovers_known_chemistry", "label": "The \u2113 term recovers known chemistry rather than revealing it", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recorded so the surviving claim is not overstated."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_chemical_scale_limit_stated", "label": "The hydride result establishes chemical-scale content only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/GENESIS-REGISTER.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Order 10\u207b\u00b9 eV over 10\u207b\u00b9\u2070 m carries no implication for nuclear-scale quantities; the boundary is enforced at register 58\u201361."}, {"id": "recovered_genesis_register_reserved_cells_addressed_vacancies", "label": "The 92 reserve